<Step id="STEP_3B_FEASIBILITY_CRITIC">
      <Goal>Reject structurally valid but operationally impossible tickets before execute. (auto)</Goal>
      <Action>
        First fold the matching persisted `FeasibilityState`. A pending `sensor-result` resumes its
        first incomplete transition below: re-present a required unresolved Ask from that result, or
        apply its recorded disposition, without dispatching, incrementing, or resetting. Only when no
        result is pending may this step dispatch ONE isolated critic with the materialized tickets, owning spec anchors,
        infra Verification Commands, and resolved phase Rules. For every phase, simulate:
        `dependency outputs + phase Target Files → one mandatory phase command (ladder + applicable §5 rows)`.
        The critic must report: a gate that needs a file owned by a later phase; a repository-wide
        fix before ignore/exclusion files exist; shared-file double ownership; an undeclared
        generator output; production entities placed in a scope without module inventory; or a test
        mapping whose code cannot exist yet.

        Persist and fold one explicit `FeasibilityState` through Gate 2 via
        `FEASIBILITY_STATE_FORMAT`; never rely on chat memory:
        `LatestTargetSet` = every materialized ticket path plus its exact latest bytes and content hash;
        `ChangedTickets` = tickets changed since the last critic result;
        `WorkerSession` = retained id and `alive|unsupported|lost` availability;
        `FallbackUsed` = boolean; `ResultCount` = cumulative critic results; `ActiveCap` = 5 or the
        operator-raised value; `ApprovedGate2Choices` = exact prior approvals;
        `PendingGate2Delta` = only a genuinely new product/toolchain fork;
        `LastResult` = literal verdict plus literal Changes. Before the first critic dispatch append
        the `opened` event. Never reset this record on Gate 2 or fallback.

        Process every critic result in this order, with no shortcut:

        | Event after a result | Mandatory transition |
        |---|---|
        | Any result | Increment `ResultCount`; append and require the complete `sensor-result` event; refresh `LatestTargetSet` and `ChangedTickets`; only then evaluate `ResultCount >= ActiveCap` BEFORE GOAL, Ask, CLEAN, fork, proceed, or re-dispatch. |
        | Active cap reached | Ask the operator per `AX_CAP_5`, regardless of verdict. If Changes is empty, offer `CLEAN`, `CONTINUE THROUGH ROUND N` with an explicit higher cap, or `RESTART: reason`; if Changes is non-empty, omit CLEAN. No automatic next result exists. |
        | Below cap + Changes non-empty | The latest bytes are unreviewed: re-dispatch; ignore any simultaneous CLEAN/fork as stale until a later no-change result reviews those bytes. |
        | Below cap + no Changes + CLEAN | The latest bytes are reviewed; proceed to STEP_4. |
        | Below cap + no Changes + new fork | Set only that fork in `PendingGate2Delta`; proceed to STEP_4 without approving it. |
        | Below cap + other no-change verdict | Apply only its ordinary ticket corrections, refresh `ChangedTickets`, and re-dispatch; unresolved/non-actionable output halts with `H_SCAFFOLD_NOT_EXECUTABLE`. |

        No cap/GOAL Ask is legal until the result/count event is durable. The Ask itself never
        mutates or replaces that event. Append the operator answer as its own immutable
        `operator-disposition` referencing the pending result before applying it. On resume, a
        pending result without that disposition re-presents the same Ask and performs no dispatch.

        Cap disposition is explicit: `CLEAN` accepts the latest no-change bytes and advances;
        `CONTINUE THROUGH ROUND N` sets `ActiveCap=N` greater than `ResultCount`, then evaluates the
        SAME `LastResult` through the below-cap rows without incrementing it twice; `RESTART: reason`
        follows that exact operator reason and is the only disposition allowed to replace this state.

        Re-dispatch into the SAME worker session whenever it is alive; only that live same-session
        path may send just `ChangedTickets`, because the session retains the unchanged target context.
        If continuation is unsupported or the retained session is lost, allow exactly ONE fresh
        fallback critic, mark `FallbackUsed`, and send the FULL `LatestTargetSet` plus the full retained
        state/context and complete prior result history; keep `ResultCount`. If that exact payload
        cannot be delivered, or a second fallback would be required, pause with a teaching
        `H_SCAFFOLD_NOT_EXECUTABLE` blocker that names the missing set/context. Never regenerate the DAG
        or all tickets, never reset the cap, and never hand off unreviewed latest bytes.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="feasibilityEvent">npx gennady sdd-session log --content-file .claude/tmp/sdd-scaffold-feasibility-event.json</ToolCall> Payload: current opened/target-refreshed/worker-state/sensor-result/operator-disposition event. Use feasibilityEvent and require success before its transition.
      </Action>
    </Step>

<Contract id="FEASIBILITY_STATE_FORMAT">
      `FeasibilityState` is not model memory. It is the fold of append-only
      `sdd-scaffold-feasibility/v1` JSON events in the compatible session's `journal:` section. The
      router has already proved/opened that session before scaffold starts, so the state survives an
      operator pause, context loss, and same-session resume without writing a second project artifact.

      Each event is one compact UTF-8 JSON line with keys in this order:
      `schema`, `cycle`, `seq`, `event`, `payload`. `cycle` binds the scaffold target-set and initial
      ticket hashes; `seq` increases by one. Event kinds are:
      `opened` (target paths/hashes, worker session, `fallbackUsed=false`, `resultCount=0`,
      `activeCap=5`) · `target-refreshed` (latest paths/hashes and changed tickets) · `worker-state` ·
      `sensor-result` (the NEW cumulative result count, literal verdict, literal Changes, and latest
      target hashes) · `operator-disposition` (the referenced result count and exact CLEAN / CONTINUE
      THROUGH ROUND N / RESTART answer) · `gate2-choice` · `closed`.

      Before the first critic dispatch, append `opened`. After every ticket mutation, append
      `target-refreshed` before dispatch. Most importantly, after a critic returns, append the complete
      `sensor-result` with the already-incremented count and require tool success BEFORE interpreting
      CLEAN, a product fork, GOAL, the cap, or emitting any Ask. An operator answer is a separate later
      immutable `operator-disposition`; never rewrite the result it disposes. On resume, fold only the
      matching cycle's events. A latest `sensor-result` with no disposition and a cap/GOAL Ask pending
      means re-present that same decision from the recorded bytes — do not redispatch, increment, or
      reset. `activeCap` starts at exactly 5 and changes only by a recorded CONTINUE disposition.

      To append any event, write that one JSON line to the regular non-symlink
      `.claude/tmp/sdd-scaffold-feasibility-event.json`, then execute the current scaffold transition's
      exact feasibility-event ToolCall. The
      successful command consumes the payload; inline event text is forbidden. `closed` is the explicit
      cleanup marker after STEP_5 integrity succeeds (or before an operator-confirmed RESTART opens a new
      cycle); the session scratch itself is removed only by its normal terminal `sdd-session close`.

    </Contract>